+            # myrmidon(G1): mode 0o600 from the first moment. The
+            # transcript holds redacted-but-still-sensitive task lines, and a bot
+            # container is shared by every profile process (one uid). The old
+            # path.write_text() created the file 0o644 & ~umask — umask 022 made it
+            # world-readable — and even an immediate chmod leaves a read window.
+            # mkstemp creates owner-only without a mode argument (0o600 regardless
+            # of umask, portable below Python 3.13), and os.replace keeps that mode;
+            # later event() appends touch an existing 0o600 file, so no window
+            # opens. A crash between create and replace unlinks the temp; the
+            # 7-day sweep would remove it anyway.
+            fd, tmp_name = tempfile.mkstemp(
